    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0480" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg412"/>

                <head>Mr. Ewing to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">The Hague</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 20, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your circular letter of the 29th March, relative to diplomatic uniform, and
                    will in future conform thereto.</p>
                <p>I take pleasure in announcing the complete evacuation by the Prussian troops of
                    the duchy of Luxembourg; which will be henceforth under the exclusive
                    sovereignty of its grand duke the King of Holland, subject to the conditions
                    imposed by the late Congress of London, that it remain neutral territory, and
                    exempt from sale or transfer.</p>
                <p>The Prussian government has called upon the grand duke to destroy the fortress;
                    the importance of which, I learn from Count Bismarck, has greatly</p>
                <p>diminished since the introduction of long-range guns.</p>
                <p>I. have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HUGH EWING.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William. H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
